{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's motion and perception as a single automaton, capturing the interaction between motion commands and obstacle sensor events. The specification enforces safe, coverage-oriented exploration: random_walk is preferred in clear states, move_forward is used for short progress, and recovery turns are used only when obstacles are detected. Recovery is conservative, with full_rotate reserved for repeated blockages. All obstacle events force a recovery turn before returning to exploration.",
  "strategy": [
    "Combine motion and perception into one plant automaton for simplicity and determinism.",
    "Specification restricts controllable actions to maximize coverage in clear states, enforce conservative recovery on obstacles, and prevent unsafe actions in obstacle states."
  ],
